{
  "id": "T-1387",
  "created_at": 1790233627.080659,
  "parent": "T-1383",
  "role": "review",
  "tier": "sonnet",
  "complexity": 7,
  "title": "review: P1: bus.create_task drops a fix round's own parent from depends_on",
  "spec": "Goal T-1383. orchestrator/bus.py create_task (bus.py:101): when constraints.fix_round_for is set and depends_on contains that same id, remove it from depends_on before saving and append a task event noting the normalization (e.g. _event(id, \"depends_on_normalized\", {\"dropped\": parent})). Other depends_on entries are kept. Why: bus.ready (bus.py:140) requires every dependency to have merged_into, and a held parent only becomes merged when its fix round merges (daemon.py report_merge walks fix_round_for), so a fix round that depends on its parent can never dispatch; headless Planners filed four such tasks in luna-inbox on 2026-09-24. Tests in tests/test_bus.py (unittest.TestCase methods): a fix round created with depends_on=[parent, other] keeps [other] and is ready once other is merged; a normal task keeps its depends_on unchanged; the normalization event is recorded.",
  "inputs": [
    "T-1384"
  ],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_bus.py::test_fix_round_drops_own_parent_from_depends_on",
    "tests/test_bus.py::test_non_fix_round_depends_on_unchanged",
    ".claude/hooks/tests-green.sh wt/<this task> exits 0"
  ],
  "scope": [
    "orchestrator/bus.py",
    "tests/test_bus.py"
  ],
  "depends_on": [],
  "constraints": {
    "read_only": true,
    "budget_turns": 20,
    "timeout_s": 900
  },
  "status": "done",
  "assigned_to": "claude:A",
  "worktree": "/Users/k3ntaw/code/orchestrator/wt/T-1387",
  "codex_thread": null,
  "result": {
    "summary": "The change in orchestrator/bus.py create_task removes fix_round_for from depends_on and keeps the other entries. It records a depends_on_normalized event with {dropped: parent}, and only after the task is saved. Both named tests are unittest.TestCase methods in tests/test_bus.py. The fix-round test checks that the kept dependency is [other], that the task is not ready until other is merged and is ready afterwards, and that the event is recorded. The non-fix test checks depends_on is unchanged and only a created event exists. Changes stay within scope. I did not run the tests. The packet says the gate passed.",
    "verdict": "approve",
